From: David Babenko-Sanders <dsanders11@electronjs.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: build: roll clang back to sub-revision 60 (UBSan CI experiment)

DO NOT MERGE. This is a CI-only experiment for the macOS UBSan
regression bisect.

The 157.0.8091.0 -> 157.0.8100.0 roll kept CLANG_REVISION at
llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b but moved CLANG_SUB_REVISION from 60 to
67 (a rebuilt clang package). Since then macOS UBSan builds report
vptr false positives in host tools such as protoc. Pin the
sub-revision back to 60 so CI's fix-sync step downloads the
sub-revision 60 package and GN's clang_revision consistency check
matches it, to tell whether the package rebuild is the cause.

diff --git a/tools/clang/scripts/update.py b/tools/clang/scripts/update.py
index 200845370e77178aa53b4176a0ea37d322d29881..07e38ef838a0a97d91c49db63a82cb8dd1a124e5 100644
--- a/tools/clang/scripts/update.py
+++ b/tools/clang/scripts/update.py
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ import zlib
 # should not be changed manually.
 # They are also read by build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn.
 CLANG_REVISION = 'llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b'
-CLANG_SUB_REVISION = 67
+CLANG_SUB_REVISION = 60
 
 PACKAGE_VERSION = '%s-%s' % (CLANG_REVISION, CLANG_SUB_REVISION)
 RELEASE_VERSION = '24'
